  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kamal Chhaparia And Ors vs The State Of Jharkhand And Anr on 30 November, 2017 Author: Rongon Mukhopadhyay Bench: Rongon Mukhopadhyay In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi Cr. M.P. No. 1876 of 2017 ---- 1. Kamal Chhaparia. 2. Binod Chhaparia. 3. Bablu Chhaparia. 4. Rishav Chhaparia. 5. Priyanka Chhaparia. 6. Bimla Devi @ Bimla Chhaparia. 7. Bina Devi @ Bina Chhaparia. 8. Monika Chhaparia. 9. Raj Kumari Chhaparia @ Raj Kumari. 10.Sweta Chhaparia. 11.Rupa Chhaparia. ....Petitioners Versus 1. The State of Jharkhand. 2. Sujit Kumar Kashsyap. .....Opposite Parties ---- Coram: Hon'Ble Mr Justice Rongon Mukhopadhyay ---------- For the Petitioners : Mr. Kaushik Sarkhel, Advocate : Mr. Nitin Kumar Pasari, Advocate",
    "facts": "It has further been submitted that without awaiting for test report, FIR has been instituted against the petitioners. It has also been submitted that steps were taken by the District Administration for cancellation of licence, which has been stayed by this Court in W.P.(C) No. 5965 of 2017.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel submits that a show cause notice was also issued to the petitioner no. 3 as to why the licence should not be cancelled, which has already been stayed by this Court. Learned counsel further submits that in view of Section 89 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2008, it can be said to have an overriding effect of this Act over all other food related laws. Learned counsel thus submits that entire criminal proceeding as against the petitioners deserves to Kamal Chhaparia And Ors vs The State Of Jharkhand And Anr on 30 November, 2017 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/19883512/ 1 be [LEAKAGE_MASK] and [LEAKAGE_MASK] in view of the aforesaid facts.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel submits that a show cause notice was also issued to the petitioner no. 3 as to why the licence should not be cancelled, which has already been stayed by this Court. Learned counsel further submits that in view of Section 89 of the Food Safety and Standard Act, 2008, it can be said to have an overriding effect of this Act over all other food related laws. Learned counsel thus submits that entire criminal proceeding as against the petitioners deserves to Kamal Chhaparia And Ors vs The State Of Jharkhand And Anr on 30 November, 2017 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/19883512/ 1 be [LEAKAGE_MASK] and [LEAKAGE_MASK] in view of the aforesaid facts.",
